Suggests: cosmic-comp, kwin-wayland, gnome-shell, hyprland, gir1.2-gtk4layershell-1.0, libgtk4-layer-shell0
Conflicts: claude-workspace
Replaces: claude-workspace
Description: workspace sidebar for COSMIC, KDE Plasma, GNOME and Hyprland, one tab per workspace
 Sidelit puts every workspace on the desktop in a sidebar on the left, one tab
 each, and finds the coding agent session working on it (Claude Code today). An
 agent's tab shows the session's title, model and directory, turns yellow when
 the agent needs you, and has a fork button; a plain workspace's tab lists what
 is open there. Clicking a tab switches to it with the keyboard in the agent's
 terminal; '+' opens a new workspace with a terminal and 'x' closes everything on
 one. The bottom of the sidebar shows the usage limits.
 .
 A daemon (a systemd user service) keeps the layout: which windows belong on
 which workspace and screen. Windows you move or close are remembered; windows
 moved by a screen change, a suspend or a login are put back, and after a login
 the sessions and windows that were open are started again.
 .
 On COSMIC it uses the ext-workspace and cosmic toplevel protocols, through a
 pure-Python Wayland client in the package; on KDE Plasma 6, KWin's D-Bus
 interface and a KWin script; on GNOME (46 and later, Wayland), a GNOME Shell
 extension in the package, which each user turns on once; on Hyprland, its IPC
 sockets. Nothing is compiled.
 The session features need the claude CLI. This package replaces
 claude-workspace, the project's earlier name.
